"{\"url\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/project/prj_1K21RKWYX1S0NWN6\",\"title\":\"Project Dourado — Isometric\",\"head\":[\"VALIDATED\",\"EW\",\"Project Dourado\",\"InPlanet\",\"->\",\"PROJECT DETAILS\",\"Expected first certificates\",\"2026\",\"Validated by\",\"350Solutions\",\"->\",\"Project code\"],\"issued_header\":null,\"buffer_header\":null,\"crediting\":null,\"verifier\":null,\"code\":\"D74G\",\"approval\":\"01 Apr 2026\",\"protocol_current\":\"Enhanced Weathering in Agriculture v1.1\",\"protocol_baseline\":null,\"cert_issued\":null,\"cert_retired\":null,\"cert_buffer\":null,\"reversal\":null,\"showing\":[\"Showing 3 of 3\"],\"tables\":[{\"heads\":[\"Submission date\",\"Title\",\"Download\"],\"rows\":[[\"01 Apr 2026\",\"Validation Report\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"09 Mar 2026\",\"Public Comment Period Summary\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"30 Jan 2026\",\"PDD\",\"PDF | ->\"]]}],\"links\":[{\"h\":\"https://inplanet.earth\",\"t\":\"InPlanet\"},{\"h\":\"https://350solutions.com\",\"t\":\"350Solutions\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/enhanced-weathering-agriculture/1.1\",\"t\":\"Enhanced Weathering in Agriculture v1.1\"},{\"h\":\"/supplier/spl_1HW7TJTRT1S0QM20\",\"t\":\"Learn more\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1HW7TJTRT1S0QM20/prj_1K21RKWYX1S0NWN6/pjd_1KN5274N31S0N7ND/validation_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1HW7TJTRT1S0QM20/prj_1K21RKWYX1S0NWN6/pjd_1KK96SBJF1S0Y2JC/public_comment_period_summary.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1HW7TJTRT1S0QM20/prj_1K21RKWYX1S0NWN6/pjd_1KG850VGJ1S0B9AZ/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"VALIDATED\\nEW\\nProject Dourado\\nInPlanet\\n->\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nExpected first certificates\\n2026\\nValidated by\\n350Solutions\\n->\\nProject code\\nD74G\\nApproval date\\n01 Apr 2026\\nCrediting period\\n10 Feb 2025 to 10 Feb 2030\\nPROTOCOL DETAILS\\nCurrent protocol version\\nEnhanced Weathering in Agriculture v1.1\\nSummary\\n\\nEnhanced Weathering project executed on agricultural land in Brazil. The purpose of the project is to remove carbon durably through the application of locally sourced basaltic rock powder whilst restoring degraded soils. Project Dourado takes its name from one of Brazil’s most iconic freshwater fish, the Dourado (Salminus brasiliensis), often called the king of the rivers. Known for its brilliant golden color and remarkable strength, the Dourado symbolizes resilience and balance in nature. Thriving only in clean, well-oxygenated rivers, it serves as a natural indicator of healthy ecosystems. In the same spirit, Project Dourado reflects InPlanet’s determination to restore ecosystems, regenerate soils, and bring balance back to our planet with permanent carbon removal.\\n\\nMato Grosso do Sul\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nEnhanced Weathering (EW) accelerates the Earth's natural chemical weathering process to remove carbon dioxide from the atmosphere. In chemical weathering, carbon dioxide dissolved in rainwater reacts with minerals in rocks, partly dissolving them and producing stable bicarbonate ions. These bicarbonate ions are transported by rivers to the ocean, where they are safely stored for thousands of years. EW is typically carried out by spreading crushed reactive rocks or minerals on croplands.\\n\\nLearn more\\nProject timeline\\nCompleted 2025\\nInitial documentation submission\\nCompleted 2025\\nAudit kick-off\\nCompleted 28 Feb 2026\\nPublic comment period\\nCompleted 2026\\nSite visit\\nCompleted 2026\\nApproval date\\nExpected 2026\\nIN PROGRESS\\nInitial credit issuance\\n\\nIsometric issues credits to the project proponent. The results of the process, including the validation and verification report, will be made available for each project on the Registry.\\n\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n01 Apr 2026\\tValidation Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n09 Mar 2026\\tPublic Comment Period Summary\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n30 Jan 2026\\tPDD\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 3 of 3\\nPrevious\\nNext\"}"